00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:21.180
A covered call ETF overlays short calls on a long equity or index position to generate premium income while retaining ownership of the underlying.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:27.540
Today's market shows elevated volatility from Fed-Hike signals and a widening trade deficit,

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:32.880
making income overlays more attractive for investors who want yield without selling shares.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:40.100
The Hamilton-enhanced Canadian-covered call ETF applies 25% leverage to a basket of Canadian dividend

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:47.520
pairs and rights-covered calls, delivering a 10.1% yield paid monthly. Investors can implement

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:54.840
this inside a TFSA by purchasing HDIV through any brokerage that offers TFX-listed ETFs,

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:01.660
then reinvesting distributions to calm the yield. The strategy performed well in sideways or mildly

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:07.300
bullish markets because the premium cushion's small declines, it caps upside when the underlying

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:12.920
rally sharply, as seen in the ETF's 12% year-to-date price gain before distributions.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:19.020
risk rises in strong bull markets because the calls may be exercised, forcing sale of

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.460
the underlying at the strike.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.720
Pair the position with the same day volume check above the 20-day average to avoid entering

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.980
when sector rotation is already underway.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:34.480
Imagine you added a small Bitcoin allocation to your TFSA last year when ETF flows turned

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:35.060
positive.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:41.120
Your purchase failed at the prevailing spot price, yet the actual cost basis also reflected

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:46.520
the ETF's management fee and any premium or discount to net asset value that day.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:51.280
Bitcoin's correlation with equities has stayed low over multi-year periods,

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:57.020
which improves the efficient frontier when the allocation stays between 1 and 5%.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:02.740
The correlation spikes during liquidity shocks and can erase that diversification benefit quickly.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:10.040
Canadian investors gain an edge by holding BTCX or ETHX inside a TFSA

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.500
because all gains remain tax-free and contribution room is preserved.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:19.800
The pro tip is to set the position size once using portfolio correlation software

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.720
and then rebalance only on a fixed schedule rather than reacting to price swings.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:29.820
Most retail investors assume any crypto holding is automatically speculative,

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:37.040
yet a 1-5% sleeve functions as a diversifier when the rest of the portfolio stays in broad equities and bonds.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.520
bonds, exceeding 5% shifts the sleeve into outright speculation.

